config_kernel.h in this directory
=================================

This is not a file of the DDK source tree. It is the configuration header the
DDK's own build system generates, pinned here because every structure layout
in include/rogue/rgx_fwif_km.h depends on it. It is copied unchanged from
binary_am62p_linux_nulldrmws_release/config_kernel.h of the DDK 25.2 tree on
the build host (sha256 in ../../UPSTREAM).

How it was produced
-------------------

The build that produced it was run in a scratch directory that no longer
exists, and its exact command line was not recorded. What is known:

- The output directory name comes from build/linux/config/core.mk line 145,
  OUT ?= $(TOP)/binary_$(PVR_BUILD_DIR)_$(WINDOW_SYSTEM)_$(BUILD),
  so the build ran with PVR_BUILD_DIR=am62p_linux, WINDOW_SYSTEM=nulldrmws,
  BUILD=release.
- The config_kernel.mk written next to it records the rest:
  KERNELDIR = a Linux 6.6.138 tree (KERNEL_ID 6.6.138-7.6.1, Toradex),
  KERNEL_CROSS_COMPILE = aarch64--glibc--stable-2024.05-1 (bootlin)
  bin/aarch64-linux-, RGX_BNC 36.V.104.796, PVR_SYSTEM rgx_ti_linux,
  KERNEL_COMPONENTS srvkm.

Following the DDK's INSTALL file and root Makefile, the corresponding command
from the DDK root is

  make PVR_BUILD_DIR=am62p_linux WINDOW_SYSTEM=nulldrmws BUILD=release \
       KERNELDIR=<linux 6.6 tree> CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-

This reconstruction has not been re-run. Some defines come from the kernel
configuration (for example PVRSRV_USE_LINUX_CONFIG_INIT_ON_ALLOC); which of
them could change a firmware-interface layout was not checked. The layouts the
driver relies on are pinned by driver/tools/offsetof/ddk_abi_check.c.

Which firmware it matches
-------------------------

It is the kernel-module configuration for the AM62P, the one TI builds next to
rgx.fw.36.53.104.796. The firmware binary is prebuilt by Imagination and its
own build configuration is not published. This header gives the structure
sizes the firmware reads (RGXFWIF_KCCB_CMD 160 bytes, RGXFWIF_FWCOMMONCONTEXT
456 bytes), which the board confirms; the DDK's copy-to-kernel-tc/config_kernel.h
gives different sizes (80 and 336) and does not match the firmware.

To compile the FWIF headers against it, force-include it (-include
config_kernel.h) with this directory on the include path; it already defines
RGX_FW_HEAP_OSID_ASSIGNMENT and PVRSRV_HWPERF_COUNTERS_PERBLK.
